1
00:00:18,567 --> 00:00:22,537
That's why I'm here to give you a warning.

2
00:00:23,539 --> 00:00:27,767
We are going to exhaust every legal remedy

3
00:00:27,767 --> 00:00:31,165
to bring Florence back to her real family.

4
00:00:32,101 --> 00:00:35,971
So you can be returned to us, the Almeros.

5
00:00:35,971 --> 00:00:39,908
So, this is not the last time
you're going to see me.

6
00:00:39,908 --> 00:00:41,666
And please...

7
00:00:41,667 --> 00:00:45,781
don't do anything
that will put you in danger.

8
00:00:45,781 --> 00:00:51,667
Or should I tell the Almeros
to stop bothering us

9
00:00:51,667 --> 00:00:55,524
and just let me be
because I'm not their missing granddaughter?

10
00:00:55,524 --> 00:01:00,162
I'm not an Almero.
I'm a Dela Cruz and that's the real me.

11
00:01:00,162 --> 00:01:03,365
That's the truth I believed, Nero.

12
00:01:03,365 --> 00:01:05,181
So whether we like it or not,

13
00:01:05,181 --> 00:01:07,752
we need to recognize the fact
that she grew up

14
00:01:07,752 --> 00:01:09,805
with a different identity,
with a different family.

15
00:01:09,805 --> 00:01:11,740
Secondly, she must come to us on her own.

16
00:01:11,740 --> 00:01:14,538
She should voluntarily come to us,

17
00:01:14,538 --> 00:01:20,832
because if we force her,
the more she'll resist being an Almero.

18
00:01:20,832 --> 00:01:23,619
You heard what Don Rogelio said, right?

19
00:01:23,619 --> 00:01:26,989
They won't stop until they get you back.

20
00:01:26,989 --> 00:01:30,259
We won't easily give in, Florence.

21
00:01:30,259 --> 00:01:34,630
We're not related but you're still my child.

22
00:01:34,630 --> 00:01:38,467
We're one family here.

23
00:01:38,467 --> 00:01:41,470
You're connected to our hearts.

24
00:01:41,470 --> 00:01:43,939
I'm the cause of this problem,

25
00:01:43,939 --> 00:01:48,544
that's why I can find a way to solve this.

26
00:01:48,544 --> 00:01:55,316
I noticed the first time I saw Florence
that she looks kind of familiar.

27
00:01:56,018 --> 00:02:01,824
She had this uncanny resemblance
to the late Alyanna Almero.

28
00:02:01,824 --> 00:02:05,094
Still, it's unbelievable...

29
00:02:05,094 --> 00:02:12,166
that the missing daughter of Lorenzo
is Florence Dela Cruz.

30
00:03:01,750 --> 00:03:03,484
Did you agree?

31
00:03:05,254 --> 00:03:07,188
Do I have a choice?

32
00:03:10,812 --> 00:03:12,761
I already talked to Grandpa Garp.

33
00:03:12,761 --> 00:03:14,863
And we have really good lawyers.

34
00:03:14,863 --> 00:03:18,023
We can help Ms. Lydia and Mr. Federico.

35
00:03:19,902 --> 00:03:24,205
Do you think I want to include
the Ferells in this mess?

36
00:03:24,940 --> 00:03:28,911
And based on the history
of both our families...

37
00:03:28,911 --> 00:03:33,114
I don't think it's good for you
to be involved with my problem right now.

38
00:03:38,791 --> 00:03:40,792
That's why you'll just agree?

39
00:03:41,890 --> 00:03:45,526
You'll agree to turn your back
on the life you've been living?

40
00:03:46,328 --> 00:03:48,830
Do you think I want this?

41
00:03:50,332 --> 00:03:54,402
Do you think
I'm not having a hard time deciding on this?

42
00:03:57,539 --> 00:04:00,676
But what can I do?

43
00:04:00,676 --> 00:04:03,745
The moment I became an Almero,

44
00:04:03,745 --> 00:04:08,316
I have to accept the big changes in my life.

45
00:04:09,651 --> 00:04:13,121
I didn't ask this for myself.

46
00:04:15,991 --> 00:04:18,993
And I didn't wish for this complication,
Nero.

47
00:04:19,861 --> 00:04:22,797
But I must recognize it.

48
00:04:23,498 --> 00:04:26,335
Because no matter what I do...

49
00:04:26,335 --> 00:04:28,836
I can't escape from it.

50
00:04:31,173 --> 00:04:32,974
That's why, Nero...

51
00:04:35,010 --> 00:04:38,012
I hope you'll understand my decision.

52
00:04:40,406 --> 00:04:44,410
I hope you'll understand
that I need to do this.

53
00:05:12,180 --> 00:05:15,250
<i>But what can I do?</i>

54
00:05:15,250 --> 00:05:21,623
<i>The moment I became an Almero,
I have to accept the big changes in my life.</i>

55
00:05:21,623 --> 00:05:25,026
<i>I didn't ask this for myself.</i>

56
00:07:19,441 --> 00:07:22,577
<i>And I didn't wish for this complication.</i>

57
00:07:22,577 --> 00:07:28,216
<i>But I must recognize it, Nero,
because no matter what I do...</i>

58
00:07:28,216 --> 00:07:30,751
<i>I can't escape from it.</i>

59
00:08:18,283 --> 00:08:21,318
I hope you'll understand my decision.

60
00:08:23,726 --> 00:08:27,863
I hope you'll understand
that I need to do this.

61
00:08:58,607 --> 00:09:00,207
How's the food?

62
00:09:02,609 --> 00:09:04,579
It's okay.

63
00:09:04,579 --> 00:09:08,216
We're sorry
that we weren't able to give you a proper welcome.

64
00:09:08,216 --> 00:09:11,453
We just need to do a lot of things
in the office.

65
00:09:11,453 --> 00:09:14,556
But if you need anything, just call Baste.

66
00:09:14,556 --> 00:09:16,490
He'll take care of everything.

67
00:09:18,138 --> 00:09:20,573
There will be some changes here.

68
00:09:22,998 --> 00:09:24,365
What?

69
00:09:25,320 --> 00:09:30,024
You need to look and act like an Almero.

70
00:09:31,373 --> 00:09:34,642
What do you mean?

71
00:09:35,477 --> 00:09:39,247
Now that you're living with us, you know...

72
00:09:39,247 --> 00:09:44,218
we have to transform you into someone worthy
to be called an Almero.

73
00:09:48,023 --> 00:09:50,257
Go ahead and eat.

74
00:10:16,489 --> 00:10:18,590
Mr. Baste...

75
00:10:19,802 --> 00:10:21,456
Are those my things?

76
00:10:21,456 --> 00:10:23,861
What are you going to do?

77
00:10:23,861 --> 00:10:26,188
I'm replacing all your old clothes
with new ones.

78
00:10:26,188 --> 00:10:27,629
Outfits that suit you better.

79
00:10:27,629 --> 00:10:30,846
And as for this,

80
00:10:30,846 --> 00:10:34,626
let's change this to a newer model
with more secure connection.

81
00:10:34,626 --> 00:10:37,595
Baste, you take care of that.

82
00:11:46,541 --> 00:11:49,844
Ms. Celestina, today we will be
fixing your posture.

83
00:11:49,844 --> 00:11:51,883
Please look ahead.

84
00:11:51,883 --> 00:11:54,352
Look ahead.

85
00:11:55,550 --> 00:11:59,742
We will be correcting your back posture.

86
00:12:01,657 --> 00:12:03,692
Okay, get a book.

87
00:12:05,874 --> 00:12:07,976
On top of your head.

88
00:12:12,818 --> 00:12:18,587
Chin up, shoulders down, stomach in.

89
00:12:18,587 --> 00:12:23,553
And one foot over the other,
gracefully and start.

90
00:12:23,553 --> 00:12:26,247
One foot over the other, gracefully.

91
00:12:26,247 --> 00:12:29,383
With great timing. One more time.

92
00:12:31,469 --> 00:12:34,348
Again, from the top. Let's go.

93
00:12:35,300 --> 00:12:37,101
Book on your head.

94
00:12:38,393 --> 00:12:40,829
Shoulders, and back straight, stomach in.

95
00:12:40,829 --> 00:12:42,147
Again.

96
00:12:42,147 --> 00:12:47,968
One... two... From the top.

97
00:12:57,074 --> 00:13:00,201
Mr. Baste, let's eat.

98
00:13:00,201 --> 00:13:02,699
Go ahead, Ma'am, it's okay.

99
00:13:03,574 --> 00:13:06,895
You know, it's fun to eat
if you have companions.

100
00:13:06,895 --> 00:13:10,107
How about your co-workers?
Maybe they want to eat too.

101
00:13:10,107 --> 00:13:12,746
Just go ahead, they've eaten already.

102
00:13:15,348 --> 00:13:17,132
Hello.

103
00:13:17,132 --> 00:13:20,191
Yes, so what's the pitch?

104
00:13:20,191 --> 00:13:22,203
Main offer?

105
00:13:22,203 --> 00:13:24,506
Try to get a better one.

106
00:13:24,506 --> 00:13:26,188
Yeah.

107
00:13:26,188 --> 00:13:28,990
Hold on, hold on... Yes?

108
00:13:28,990 --> 00:13:31,045
Okay, go ahead.
I just have to take this call.

109
00:13:31,045 --> 00:13:32,340
Hello.

110
00:13:33,198 --> 00:13:35,326
Hold on...

111
00:13:36,818 --> 00:13:40,349
If you want, next week,
let's make plans with your grandfather.

112
00:13:40,349 --> 00:13:41,489
Let's go out of town.

113
00:13:41,489 --> 00:13:44,349
Not this week, I'm really busy, okay?

114
00:13:44,349 --> 00:13:45,552
All right.

115
00:13:45,552 --> 00:13:46,728
Hello.

116
00:13:46,728 --> 00:13:49,324
Yes, yes. Let's finish it this week.

117
00:14:16,996 --> 00:14:22,096
I will knock, knock and knock
until he opens the door.

118
00:14:22,096 --> 00:14:24,818
If he refuses to open the door,
I will destroy it.

119
00:14:24,818 --> 00:14:27,107
If I need to sneak into the house

120
00:14:27,107 --> 00:14:29,873
or peek through the window
so he'll let me in,

121
00:14:29,873 --> 00:14:31,254
I'll do it.

122
00:14:31,254 --> 00:14:33,716
If I need to shout, I will shout...

123
00:14:33,716 --> 00:14:38,373
Hey, let me in your heart!

124
00:14:38,373 --> 00:14:41,382
Hey, let me in your heart.

125
00:14:41,382 --> 00:14:42,584
Let me in!

126
00:14:42,584 --> 00:14:45,927
For this kind of beauty you're not expecting,
like me.

127
00:14:45,927 --> 00:14:48,763
If he still refuses to let you in,
I don't know how else.

128
00:14:52,627 --> 00:14:56,964
You're asking what my favorite fruit is.

129
00:14:58,939 --> 00:15:00,707
It's rambutan.

130
00:15:08,676 --> 00:15:11,079
Hey, don't be noisy.

131
00:15:11,079 --> 00:15:13,274
As if I'm a stranger to you

132
00:15:13,274 --> 00:15:18,186
when you go to me every morning
to bring messages.

133
00:15:18,186 --> 00:15:19,654
You're surprised.

134
00:15:19,654 --> 00:15:22,556
I know your boss' secret.

135
00:15:24,524 --> 00:15:30,670
He thinks he's the only one capable
of sending secret messages.

136
00:15:30,670 --> 00:15:32,990
If he's sending secret messages,

137
00:15:32,990 --> 00:15:34,869
I give secret fruits.

138
00:15:34,869 --> 00:15:36,737
Rambutan.

139
00:15:53,855 --> 00:15:55,948
You owe me.

140
00:15:57,926 --> 00:15:59,494
How much?

141
00:15:59,494 --> 00:16:02,512
Do I have to pay for your cabin?

142
00:16:02,512 --> 00:16:05,560
I don't need your money.

143
00:16:05,560 --> 00:16:07,235
Huh?

144
00:16:07,235 --> 00:16:10,171
So what do I owe you?

145
00:16:10,171 --> 00:16:13,019
You owe me three P's.

146
00:16:14,023 --> 00:16:15,655
Three P's?

147
00:16:17,178 --> 00:16:19,614
Pantawid Pangkabuhayan Program?

148
00:16:19,614 --> 00:16:23,918
What I mean is, you owe me three favors.

149
00:16:23,918 --> 00:16:25,787
Three favors?

150
00:16:25,787 --> 00:16:27,422
Yes.

151
00:16:27,422 --> 00:16:30,712
When the time comes
that I need a favor from you,

152
00:16:30,712 --> 00:16:32,707
you can't refuse.

153
00:16:32,707 --> 00:16:34,483
No questions asked.

154
00:16:34,483 --> 00:16:37,298
You'll just help me
with the favors that I need from you.

155
00:16:37,298 --> 00:16:39,571
What kind of favor?

156
00:16:39,571 --> 00:16:42,140
Anything.

157
00:16:43,338 --> 00:16:44,891
As in anything?

158
00:16:44,891 --> 00:16:46,558
Yes.

159
00:16:48,843 --> 00:16:50,945
Anything.

160
00:16:50,945 --> 00:16:52,980
That's enough.

161
00:16:56,150 --> 00:17:01,218
It's impossible that you saw her yesterday,
so that's not true.

162
00:17:02,490 --> 00:17:04,792
What makes you say that?

163
00:17:06,761 --> 00:17:11,431
Because we were together yesterday.

164
00:17:14,816 --> 00:17:16,104
She's my girlfriend.

165
00:17:16,104 --> 00:17:18,038
What?

166
00:18:11,548 --> 00:18:15,574
Shall we, my Chummy pie?

167
00:18:52,867 --> 00:18:54,102
Lie down.

168
00:18:54,102 --> 00:18:55,833
Lie down, here.

169
00:19:06,452 --> 00:19:07,986
I said lie down.

170
00:19:14,189 --> 00:19:16,357
Lie down.

171
00:19:16,357 --> 00:19:19,894
Just wait. Excuse me.

172
00:19:19,894 --> 00:19:21,561
There you go.

173
00:19:22,330 --> 00:19:24,732
Are you ready?

174
00:19:24,732 --> 00:19:26,667
I said, are you ready?

175
00:19:26,667 --> 00:19:28,536
I'll count to three.

176
00:19:28,536 --> 00:19:32,373
One, two, three.

177
00:19:32,373 --> 00:19:34,041
- You pervert!
- Hey, what's that?

178
00:19:34,041 --> 00:19:35,076
- You're crazy!
- Ouch.

179
00:19:35,076 --> 00:19:37,645
- You pervert! You're planning something!
- What do you mean?

180
00:19:37,645 --> 00:19:39,160
- I'm planning something?
- You're planning something bad.

181
00:19:39,160 --> 00:19:40,915
- What?
- Wait, wait...

182
00:19:40,915 --> 00:19:42,950
Just calm down. Okay, just calm down.

183
00:19:42,950 --> 00:19:43,951
- Calm down.
- What is it?

184
00:19:43,951 --> 00:19:44,952
Wait, here it is.

185
00:19:44,952 --> 00:19:46,487
What do you have in there?

186
00:19:46,487 --> 00:19:48,589
- You will kill me?
- I don't have any evil plans.

187
00:19:48,589 --> 00:19:51,692
Wait. I'm not planning something bad. Here.

188
00:19:54,474 --> 00:19:56,074
What's that?

189
00:20:02,751 --> 00:20:04,472
- There
- There.

190
00:20:04,472 --> 00:20:05,872
There.

191
00:20:07,890 --> 00:20:10,511
Orionids meteor shower.

192
00:20:10,511 --> 00:20:13,347
Those are remnants of the Halley's comet.

193
00:20:13,347 --> 00:20:18,673
Imagine, the last time we saw Halley
was in 1986.

194
00:20:19,548 --> 00:20:24,618
But even right now now,
we can still feel its presence.

195
00:20:28,663 --> 00:20:32,306
I hope I have that impact
on the person I love.

196
00:20:33,701 --> 00:20:36,737
That even if I'm no longer around...

197
00:20:36,737 --> 00:20:41,196
she will still remember
the beautiful memories I left for her.

198
00:20:43,299 --> 00:20:45,259
Is it beautiful?

199
00:20:45,259 --> 00:20:47,854
It's beautiful.

200
00:20:47,854 --> 00:20:49,855
Beautiful.

201
00:20:56,585 --> 00:20:59,887
Yes, it's beautiful.

202
00:21:04,599 --> 00:21:06,935
Go ahead and see if it's beautiful.

203
00:21:06,935 --> 00:21:08,603
Okay.

204
00:21:21,632 --> 00:21:23,767
It's really beautiful.

205
00:21:25,912 --> 00:21:30,899
Yes, it's so beautiful.

206
00:21:35,311 --> 00:21:37,446
Let's share.

207
00:21:38,887 --> 00:21:41,641
Okay, you can use the other side.

208
00:21:52,403 --> 00:21:54,972
I hope you like it.

209
00:22:01,173 --> 00:22:03,908
Is that special delivery?

210
00:22:06,020 --> 00:22:08,488
Thank you, Nero.

211
00:22:10,139 --> 00:22:13,609
I know you're always there for me.

212
00:22:15,376 --> 00:22:18,331
Thank you for the falling star.

213
00:22:45,974 --> 00:22:47,541
How is she?

214
00:22:48,439 --> 00:22:51,132
We haven't talked to each other.

215
00:22:51,133 --> 00:22:53,087
Why, did you fight?

216
00:22:53,087 --> 00:22:54,399
We didn't.

217
00:22:54,400 --> 00:22:57,533
I tried to call her but she cannot be reached.

218
00:22:57,533 --> 00:22:59,768
She really can't be reached

219
00:22:59,768 --> 00:23:04,618
because she's not just rich,
she is very rich.

220
00:23:10,371 --> 00:23:11,497
Too early?

221
00:23:11,497 --> 00:23:12,583
Yes.

222
00:23:12,583 --> 00:23:13,910
Okay.

223
00:23:13,910 --> 00:23:17,932
Maybe her signal is weak in Almero's mansion.

224
00:23:17,932 --> 00:23:19,169
I don't think so.

225
00:23:19,169 --> 00:23:23,604
If they don't have a 5G signal,
at least they have WiFi in the mansion.

226
00:23:23,604 --> 00:23:27,949
I don't think
it's a matter of WiFi or signal.

227
00:23:27,949 --> 00:23:31,092
Knowing Rogelio...

228
00:23:31,092 --> 00:23:35,182
They took away Florence's cell phone.

229
00:23:35,182 --> 00:23:38,151
Why would they do that, Grandpa?

230
00:23:39,049 --> 00:23:44,707
You must understand, Nero,
that the Almeros are a very proud family.

231
00:23:44,707 --> 00:23:48,128
They are one of the oldest families.

232
00:23:48,128 --> 00:23:53,067
And they are very sensitive
with their reputation.

233
00:23:53,067 --> 00:23:56,836
And now that Florence is with them,

234
00:23:57,972 --> 00:24:02,242
I'm sure she's going to be changed
and become an Almero.

235
00:24:02,242 --> 00:24:06,914
And this change is not
just going to be physical.

236
00:24:06,914 --> 00:24:09,300
Unfortunately, this means

237
00:24:09,300 --> 00:24:15,400
Florence now is being forced
to forget the life that she had.

238
00:24:15,400 --> 00:24:17,133
She is now an Almero

239
00:24:17,133 --> 00:24:22,896
and she needs to forget
her life being a Dela Cruz.

240
00:24:30,437 --> 00:24:32,549
- What's taking them so long?
- They're coming.

241
00:24:32,549 --> 00:24:33,687
- Huh?
- Don't be impatient.

242
00:24:33,687 --> 00:24:35,890
They'll come.

243
00:24:35,890 --> 00:24:37,691
What time is it?

244
00:24:37,691 --> 00:24:39,360
You don't have a watch.

245
00:24:39,360 --> 00:24:40,407
What time is it?

246
00:24:40,407 --> 00:24:43,564
- Hey, Dencio.
- Hey, Federico and Lydia.

247
00:24:43,564 --> 00:24:45,258
Thank you for coming here.

248
00:24:45,258 --> 00:24:48,169
Welcome!

249
00:24:48,169 --> 00:24:49,366
- Welcome!
- Go ahead and repeat it.

250
00:24:49,366 --> 00:24:51,271
Repeat it.

251
00:24:53,921 --> 00:24:57,011
Are you sure about what you're saying?

252
00:24:57,011 --> 00:24:59,947
Yes, maybe you're just scamming us.

253
00:24:59,947 --> 00:25:02,917
Don Ferell's offer is not a scam.

254
00:25:02,917 --> 00:25:06,421
It was he who asked for you
to be the cook here in the mansion.

255
00:25:06,421 --> 00:25:12,449
As a matter of fact,
it wasn't Don Ferell who said it.

256
00:25:12,449 --> 00:25:15,402
The person who said this was...

257
00:25:19,488 --> 00:25:21,035
Mother, Father.

258
00:25:21,035 --> 00:25:23,303
- Nero.
- Nero.

259
00:25:29,535 --> 00:25:32,713
And we are back.

260
00:25:32,713 --> 00:25:38,385
Welcome back to GU TV
with a capital G for you and me.

261
00:25:38,385 --> 00:25:41,922
So, fellow G's, how was your academic break?

262
00:25:41,922 --> 00:25:44,623
Were you able to do something worthwhile?

263
00:25:44,623 --> 00:25:47,929
Actually, you know what,
Gyronella is so unique.

264
00:25:47,929 --> 00:25:50,431
And one of the things that makes us unique

265
00:25:50,431 --> 00:25:52,887
is that we have an academic break
for students

266
00:25:52,887 --> 00:25:57,316
because it truly is the belief
of our founding fathers and mothers

267
00:25:57,316 --> 00:25:59,540
that the best way to shape a young mind

268
00:25:59,540 --> 00:26:04,211
is to set them free
from the confines of the classroom.

269
00:26:04,211 --> 00:26:06,114
Which begs the question...

270
00:26:06,114 --> 00:26:09,909
Why are we paying thousands and
thousands of pesos in tuition fees

271
00:26:09,909 --> 00:26:14,020
if we'll learn a lot of things
from going out?

272
00:26:14,901 --> 00:26:18,520
But that is not the question
that needs answering

273
00:26:18,520 --> 00:26:24,865
because the more important question is,
what's the G?

274
00:26:24,865 --> 00:26:27,989
And the biggest G of our university now

275
00:26:27,989 --> 00:26:32,640
sounds like the biggest plot point
of a novel.

276
00:26:32,640 --> 00:26:34,541
Are you guys ready?

277
00:26:35,676 --> 00:26:37,299
Rumor has it

278
00:26:37,300 --> 00:26:41,132
that the Communication Arts Representative

279
00:26:41,133 --> 00:26:47,588
is the only daughter
of one of the most influential families...

280
00:26:47,588 --> 00:26:50,588
The Almeros!

281
00:26:50,588 --> 00:26:52,645
Are you guys surprised?

282
00:26:52,645 --> 00:26:57,130
Because I am... OMG!

283
00:26:58,232 --> 00:27:01,769
You know buddy, it's okay here.
The benefits here are good.

284
00:27:01,769 --> 00:27:02,936
You have SSS.

285
00:27:02,936 --> 00:27:04,238
GSIS.

286
00:27:04,238 --> 00:27:06,354
And DSWD.

287
00:27:06,354 --> 00:27:09,109
See, there are a lot of benefits here.

288
00:27:09,109 --> 00:27:12,541
Include the benefit of the doubt too.

289
00:27:12,541 --> 00:27:14,180
Hey...

290
00:27:17,217 --> 00:27:18,385
Grandpa.

291
00:27:18,385 --> 00:27:24,425
Don Ferell, thank you very much
for your offer.

292
00:27:24,425 --> 00:27:28,208
Yes, we just need a little distraction

293
00:27:28,208 --> 00:27:31,932
because there are a lot of memories at home.

294
00:27:31,932 --> 00:27:34,601
That's why, thank you very much, Don Ferell.

295
00:27:34,601 --> 00:27:39,140
Buddy, just call Don Ferell Grandpa Garp.

296
00:27:39,140 --> 00:27:42,476
Yes, a lot of people might hear you

297
00:27:42,476 --> 00:27:48,147
and think that Don Ferell is an old man
in an old drama series.

298
00:27:51,452 --> 00:27:54,207
Welcome to the house.

299
00:27:54,207 --> 00:27:57,802
You know,
we're excited to taste your brand of cooking.

300
00:27:57,802 --> 00:28:01,061
Yes, if you don't mind my saying.

301
00:28:01,061 --> 00:28:05,848
We expect a lot from you
because Florence has set the bar too high.

302
00:28:08,970 --> 00:28:12,871
I'm sorry. I didn't mean it.

303
00:28:12,871 --> 00:28:15,035
That's okay, Ma'am Serafica.

304
00:28:15,035 --> 00:28:18,178
We just miss Florence.

305
00:28:18,178 --> 00:28:21,879
Nero, were you able to talk to Florence?

306
00:28:21,879 --> 00:28:25,451
I can no longer call her at her old number.

307
00:28:27,870 --> 00:28:31,606
I think she changed her number.

308
00:28:32,754 --> 00:28:35,716
Maybe she's just busy,
that's why she wasn't able to call, right?

309
00:28:35,716 --> 00:28:37,351
Yes.

310
00:28:40,042 --> 00:28:44,379
I'm sure there are a lot of changes
in her life.

311
00:28:45,672 --> 00:28:49,636
But don't worry.

312
00:28:49,636 --> 00:28:51,578
The academic break will be over soon,

313
00:28:51,578 --> 00:28:55,949
and I'm sure we'll see each other in school.

314
00:28:55,949 --> 00:28:58,490
I'll keep you updated.

315
00:29:15,540 --> 00:29:18,191
Let's go together.

316
00:29:22,743 --> 00:29:25,982
Well, well, well.

317
00:29:25,982 --> 00:29:28,382
Troy still looks fun.

318
00:29:28,382 --> 00:29:30,591
You said it.

319
00:29:30,591 --> 00:29:34,193
Excuse me, girls, but Troy is off-limits.

320
00:29:34,193 --> 00:29:36,318
- Oh.
- Okay.

321
00:29:36,318 --> 00:29:40,390
By the way, how was your trip
with Tristan to Seoul?

322
00:29:40,390 --> 00:29:45,432
Well, we were shining through the city
with a lot of fun and soul.

323
00:29:45,432 --> 00:29:49,536
The only thing I can say is, it is dynamite!

324
00:29:49,536 --> 00:29:53,573
Speaking of dynamite, here is mine.

325
00:29:53,573 --> 00:29:55,508
It's Aldus.

326
00:29:57,110 --> 00:29:58,650
You're saying "mine" as if...

327
00:29:58,650 --> 00:30:01,552
why do you have a title already for him?

328
00:30:03,350 --> 00:30:06,383
How about Owen?

329
00:30:08,205 --> 00:30:13,276
It seems like he's handling things
pretty well.

330
00:30:15,766 --> 00:30:18,786
Ooh...

331
00:30:18,786 --> 00:30:21,601
Why are you smiling like that?

332
00:30:21,601 --> 00:30:24,338
Do you like Owen?

333
00:30:24,338 --> 00:30:25,839
Of course not.

334
00:30:25,839 --> 00:30:28,326
I'm avoiding things like that

335
00:30:28,326 --> 00:30:31,946
ever since everything that happened
between Nero and I.

336
00:30:31,946 --> 00:30:36,749
Speaking of Nero,
do we have news about Florence?

337
00:30:36,749 --> 00:30:40,601
Is it true
what's happening between her and the Almeros?

338
00:30:40,601 --> 00:30:44,596
I can't wait to talk to Florence
to know the deal.

339
00:30:44,596 --> 00:30:46,264
Me too.

340
00:31:34,493 --> 00:31:35,871
Florence, can we talk?

341
00:31:35,871 --> 00:31:37,144
Can we talk later?

342
00:31:37,144 --> 00:31:40,114
I'll find a way to talk to you.

343
00:31:40,114 --> 00:31:42,574
We're your friends, Florence.
We're not a threat.

344
00:31:42,574 --> 00:31:43,717
Are you okay?

345
00:31:43,717 --> 00:31:44,752
- Are they treating you well?
- Hey Mister, that's enough.

346
00:31:44,752 --> 00:31:46,687
Hey, that's enough.

347
00:31:46,687 --> 00:31:48,455
Mister, they're not my enemies.

348
00:31:48,455 --> 00:31:49,690
- Don't do that.
- Don't!

349
00:31:49,690 --> 00:31:52,792
I said don't push us.

350
00:31:58,553 --> 00:32:00,087
Let's go.

351
00:32:06,278 --> 00:32:09,247
Oh my God, there's trouble.

352
00:32:10,073 --> 00:32:11,856
What's happening?

353
00:32:11,856 --> 00:32:13,467
I don't know the full details,

354
00:32:13,467 --> 00:32:14,629
but what I heard...

355
00:32:14,629 --> 00:32:18,618
is that her father and grandfather think
that she's in danger,

356
00:32:18,618 --> 00:32:22,262
that's why security is so tight around her.

357
00:32:22,262 --> 00:32:24,707
Why? Why would she be in danger?

358
00:32:24,707 --> 00:32:25,996
Yeah?

359
00:32:25,996 --> 00:32:29,653
Back in the day,
somebody tried to murder her and her mother.

360
00:32:29,653 --> 00:32:34,014
So since the case of her real mom
is still unsolved,

361
00:32:34,014 --> 00:32:38,334
that's probably why the Almeros are taking
great safety precautions

362
00:32:38,334 --> 00:32:39,952
for her.

363
00:32:43,516 --> 00:32:45,317
See?

364
00:32:46,226 --> 00:32:49,696
Do you see
how troublesome the Ferell guys are?

365
00:32:49,696 --> 00:32:51,431
This is symptomatic of who they are.

366
00:32:51,431 --> 00:32:53,200
They don't have respect.

367
00:32:53,200 --> 00:32:55,702
They think the whole Levante is their kingdom

368
00:32:55,702 --> 00:32:58,487
and that they own everything.

369
00:32:59,973 --> 00:33:03,677
Maybe there was just miscommunication.

370
00:33:03,677 --> 00:33:05,612
And you even managed to defend them.

371
00:33:05,612 --> 00:33:07,214
So who's at fault here?

372
00:33:07,214 --> 00:33:07,973
Is it you?

373
00:33:07,974 --> 00:33:10,299
Should you be blamed
for everything that happened?

374
00:33:10,300 --> 00:33:12,251
Lorenzo...

375
00:33:14,054 --> 00:33:16,221
Celestina, you have to understand...

376
00:33:16,221 --> 00:33:20,259
you shouldn't trust the Ferells!

377
00:33:20,994 --> 00:33:26,233
But I lived with them for a long time,
that's why I'm close to them.

378
00:33:26,233 --> 00:33:29,403
And we're going to the same school.

379
00:33:29,403 --> 00:33:32,924
I will still encounter them no matter what.

380
00:33:34,708 --> 00:33:36,109
You're right.

381
00:33:36,109 --> 00:33:38,745
You can't avoid them.

382
00:33:39,446 --> 00:33:43,617
So I think it's about time
that I transfer you to a different school.

383
00:33:43,617 --> 00:33:46,620
Look, let's not overreact, Lorenzo.

384
00:33:46,620 --> 00:33:48,355
The school started already,

385
00:33:48,355 --> 00:33:52,348
it'll be such a pity
if you waste what Florence has started in GU.

386
00:33:52,348 --> 00:33:56,510
Maybe we just have
to make Florence understand...

387
00:33:56,510 --> 00:33:59,663
that you have to cut all ties
with the Ferells.

388
00:33:59,663 --> 00:34:05,001
Because a Ferell is never good news
to this family.

389
00:34:06,864 --> 00:34:09,343
I'm not naive.

390
00:34:09,343 --> 00:34:13,139
I know all
about you and that Ferell boy, Nero.

391
00:34:13,139 --> 00:34:18,049
Yes, your grandfather told me
about your shenanigans during the ball.

392
00:34:18,049 --> 00:34:19,920
Is he your boyfriend?

393
00:34:19,920 --> 00:34:22,289
It doesn't matter.

394
00:34:22,289 --> 00:34:27,494
Because I will never allow that relationship.

395
00:34:27,494 --> 00:34:31,465
And I will never accept a Ferell
to be a part of this family!

396
00:34:31,465 --> 00:34:33,710
Now, if you refuse to listen to me

397
00:34:33,710 --> 00:34:38,343
and continue your relationship
with the Ferell guy,

398
00:34:38,343 --> 00:34:42,914
I will pull you out of your university
and send you abroad.

399
00:34:44,069 --> 00:34:46,504
I have good news for you.

400
00:34:49,255 --> 00:34:51,648
Wait, it seems my timing is wrong.

401
00:34:51,648 --> 00:34:54,921
I'm sorry if I intrude on this family matter.

402
00:34:54,921 --> 00:34:56,359
Okay, I'll just come back...

403
00:34:56,359 --> 00:34:58,692
No, no, just stay, Samuel.

404
00:34:58,692 --> 00:35:01,395
Lorenzo is done already.

405
00:35:01,395 --> 00:35:07,300
And I want an update on the dealings
with the Marquezes.

406
00:35:07,300 --> 00:35:08,969
Go to your room.

407
00:35:08,969 --> 00:35:11,646
Think carefully about what I told you.

408
00:35:21,834 --> 00:35:25,366
I'm very disappointed with you, boys.

409
00:35:25,366 --> 00:35:31,881
What went into your minds to fight with them?

410
00:35:32,815 --> 00:35:37,030
Ms. Serafica, we only wanted
to talk to Florence.

411
00:35:37,030 --> 00:35:40,033
And you too, you're the eldest.

412
00:35:40,033 --> 00:35:43,870
You should've recognized the situation.

413
00:35:44,838 --> 00:35:49,141
Are you all aware of what I mean?

414
00:35:51,311 --> 00:35:54,748
Florence's situation is different now.

415
00:35:54,748 --> 00:35:58,885
We all should be aware of the fact
that she's an Almero.

416
00:35:58,885 --> 00:36:01,670
And we're the Ferells.

417
00:36:01,670 --> 00:36:04,896
And this kind of incident

418
00:36:04,896 --> 00:36:10,796
would only complicate our relationship
with Florence.

419
00:36:13,240 --> 00:36:17,224
Boys, you have to be careful.

420
00:36:17,224 --> 00:36:20,501
There are a lot of changes in her life.

421
00:36:20,501 --> 00:36:24,010
You know, I could feel what you're feeling.

422
00:36:24,010 --> 00:36:26,467
She's close to us, right?

423
00:36:26,467 --> 00:36:33,021
But I hope we won't add
to what she's going through right now.

424
00:36:33,021 --> 00:36:34,754
That's right!

425
00:36:35,489 --> 00:36:38,325
Violence is never the answer.

426
00:36:38,325 --> 00:36:43,662
That's why give chance a peace.

427
00:36:43,662 --> 00:36:46,122
Give peace a chance.

428
00:36:46,122 --> 00:36:47,900
That's the same.

429
00:36:50,552 --> 00:36:52,888
How's the fight, boys?

430
00:36:52,888 --> 00:36:54,740
Did you do it?

431
00:36:57,089 --> 00:36:59,991
Did you do what I asked you to do?

432
00:37:01,255 --> 00:37:03,304
Of course, Grandpa.

433
00:37:03,304 --> 00:37:08,008
I'm really disappointed, Don Ferell.

434
00:37:09,422 --> 00:37:14,361
Do you believe that violence is the answer?

435
00:37:14,361 --> 00:37:19,804
You're not giving a chance a peace.

436
00:37:19,804 --> 00:37:21,968
Give peace a chance.

437
00:37:21,968 --> 00:37:23,303
I said that's the same.

438
00:37:23,303 --> 00:37:27,656
Are you really consenting your grandchildren
to become violent?

439
00:37:31,906 --> 00:37:36,212
I am also disappointed.

440
00:37:36,212 --> 00:37:40,520
As my father figure and my boss,

441
00:37:40,520 --> 00:37:46,292
I am very, very disappointed.

442
00:37:49,689 --> 00:37:52,373
Didn't you tell them?

443
00:37:53,206 --> 00:37:54,606
Huh?

444
00:37:56,403 --> 00:38:00,373
Of course, I will not tolerate violence.

445
00:38:03,810 --> 00:38:08,582
The trouble earlier was all part of a plan.

446
00:38:08,582 --> 00:38:11,137
Oh?

447
00:38:11,137 --> 00:38:12,118
Plan.

448
00:38:12,118 --> 00:38:13,823
What plan?

449
00:39:10,810 --> 00:39:12,154
Hello.

450
00:39:12,979 --> 00:39:14,648
<i>Hello, Florence.</i>

451
00:39:14,648 --> 00:39:18,018
- Surprise!
- Surprise!

452
00:39:18,018 --> 00:39:20,120
Nero?

453
00:39:20,120 --> 00:39:22,190
Is that you?

454
00:39:22,190 --> 00:39:25,626
And am I hearing the right thing?

455
00:39:25,626 --> 00:39:27,556
Yes, it's me.

456
00:39:27,556 --> 00:39:32,104
We're all complete, plus the four fools.

457
00:39:32,104 --> 00:39:34,200
And Ms. Serafica and Grandpa Garp.

458
00:39:34,200 --> 00:39:38,305
Wait, how were you able
to put the phone in my bag?

459
00:39:38,305 --> 00:39:39,526
Are they treating you well?

460
00:39:39,526 --> 00:39:40,573
- Don't push!
- What's with you?

461
00:39:40,573 --> 00:39:43,665
- Hey!
- Mister, they are my friends.

462
00:39:43,665 --> 00:39:45,679
- They're not my enemies.
- Stop it, mister.

463
00:39:45,679 --> 00:39:46,946
- Enough!
- Ouch!

464
00:39:46,946 --> 00:39:48,038
- Stop it!
- That's enough!

465
00:39:48,038 --> 00:39:50,624
- Stop!
- Stop!

466
00:39:52,530 --> 00:39:57,062
<i>Do you think
I will just let them take you away from me?</i>

467
00:39:59,343 --> 00:40:01,134
Did you see my moves earlier?

468
00:40:01,134 --> 00:40:02,437
That was nothing.

469
00:40:02,437 --> 00:40:05,882
That's no match with my muscles.

470
00:40:05,882 --> 00:40:08,201
We did all of that for you, Florence.

471
00:40:08,201 --> 00:40:13,052
I'm so impressed with you,
and I'm so touched by your efforts.

472
00:40:13,052 --> 00:40:14,632
Really?

473
00:40:14,632 --> 00:40:15,996
You're so touched?

474
00:40:15,996 --> 00:40:19,344
As in touched for the very first time?

475
00:40:19,344 --> 00:40:21,381
Fool.

476
00:40:21,381 --> 00:40:22,934
<i>Florence.</i>

477
00:40:23,783 --> 00:40:25,051
Grandpa Garp.

478
00:40:25,051 --> 00:40:26,418
Before Nero talks to you in private,

479
00:40:26,418 --> 00:40:31,057
we'd like you to know
that you're always in our hearts and minds.

480
00:40:31,057 --> 00:40:34,132
You're always in our hearts and minds.

481
00:40:34,133 --> 00:40:37,967
It should be,
because if I'm not in your hearts and minds,

482
00:40:37,967 --> 00:40:39,852
I'll feel bad.

483
00:40:41,251 --> 00:40:43,837
<i>We will never give up on you.</i>

484
00:40:43,837 --> 00:40:45,467
I would like to apologize

485
00:40:45,467 --> 00:40:48,585
for the stressed caused
by the commotion earlier.

486
00:40:48,585 --> 00:40:50,786
At first, I was hesitant,

487
00:40:50,786 --> 00:40:55,758
<i>but we needed to find a way to talk to you.</i>

488
00:40:55,758 --> 00:40:59,575
I told you,
you're already part of this family,

489
00:40:59,575 --> 00:41:02,803
<i>and we will not easily give up on you.</i>

490
00:41:02,803 --> 00:41:06,181
Florence, were you able
to eat properly there?

491
00:41:06,181 --> 00:41:08,962
Yes, Ma'am Serafica, don't worry.

492
00:41:08,962 --> 00:41:11,651
They have a cook here,

493
00:41:11,651 --> 00:41:14,279
but she's not as good as Mother and Father.

494
00:41:14,279 --> 00:41:16,466
But it's okay.

495
00:41:16,466 --> 00:41:17,644
<i>Florence,</i>

496
00:41:17,644 --> 00:41:19,417
this is Dencio.

497
00:41:19,417 --> 00:41:22,155
What, is someone fighting with you there?

498
00:41:22,155 --> 00:41:26,384
No, Mr. Dencio. I'm the bully here.

499
00:41:27,385 --> 00:41:29,044
That's good to hear, Florence,

500
00:41:29,044 --> 00:41:32,411
because if not,
I'll send a reinforcement there.

501
00:41:32,411 --> 00:41:34,900
Hey this guy,
you're sending a reinforcement that soon?

502
00:41:38,311 --> 00:41:41,621
Actually, Florence, there's still someone
who wants to talk to you.

503
00:41:41,621 --> 00:41:45,659
Who? Is that Mr. James?
Is he eating your ham?

504
00:41:45,659 --> 00:41:48,291
Tell him it's okay
as long as he's eating a half cup of rice.

505
00:41:48,291 --> 00:41:50,864
Or is it Ms. Patotina?

506
00:41:50,864 --> 00:41:53,820
Is she taking care of Ma'am Serafica?

507
00:41:56,385 --> 00:41:58,131
Hello, Florence.

508
00:41:59,339 --> 00:42:01,342
Why?

509
00:42:01,342 --> 00:42:03,576
Do you miss me already?

510
00:42:04,843 --> 00:42:08,642
Nero, we need to talk.

511
00:42:08,642 --> 00:42:11,111
How was your sleep? Is it okay?

512
00:42:11,111 --> 00:42:13,722
The truth is,
I wasn't able to sleep last night.

513
00:42:13,722 --> 00:42:16,458
I keep thinking about what Don Ferell said.

514
00:42:16,458 --> 00:42:19,586
We should find out who killed Alyanna.

515
00:42:19,586 --> 00:42:22,556
Don't you remember anything, Federico?
Anything?

516
00:42:22,556 --> 00:42:23,300
Just a little.

517
00:42:23,300 --> 00:42:27,186
Maybe I can remember
the shape of the head, the shape of his eyes.

518
00:42:27,186 --> 00:42:29,969
If there's a suspect,
they make a drawing, right?

519
00:42:29,969 --> 00:42:31,671
Yes, that's right. There's a name for that.

520
00:42:31,671 --> 00:42:36,042
Cartographic sketch artist.

521
00:42:36,042 --> 00:42:37,604
Yes, that's the one.

522
00:42:37,604 --> 00:42:41,142
Why do you need to talk to me
if I didn't do anything bad?

523
00:42:41,142 --> 00:42:45,951
It's because
someone wants to talk to you, Florence.

524
00:42:53,493 --> 00:42:59,937
Is it true that you have something to do
with what happened to Mommy?
